        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": " $ \\Psi_k, \\ldots, \\Psi_m $. Subsequently, formula (2.8) will be applied to obtain the generalized Jordan vectors of the corresponding root function  $ \\hat{\\phi}(z) $.",
