        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "According to the converse part of Theorem 2.1, solving equations (2.2) and (2.3) does not guarantee that a pole cancellation function of exact order  $ k $ is obtained. Only if one can select a solution satisfying  $ \\Psi_k \\neq 0 $ does one obtain a pole cancellation function of exact order  $ k $.",
            "block_bbox": [
                231,
                285,
                958,
                386
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    231.0,
                    285.0
                ],
                [
                    958.0,
                    285.0
                ],
                [
                    958.0,
                    386.0
                ],
                [
                    231.0,
                    386.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "In the case  $ k = m $, condition (2.6) will be used to determine  $ \\Psi_m \\neq 0 $.",
            "block_bbox": [
                255,
