        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Observe that the pole cancellation function  $ \\Psi(z) $ cannot be of order  $ k > m $, since in that case condition (a) in Definition 1.2 would not be satisfied. This is why, in conditions (2.2), (2.3), (2.6), and formula (2.8), only the coefficients of the principal part of the Laurent expansion of  $ Q(z) $ around the pole  $ \\beta = 1 $ are used.",
            "block_bbox": [
                230,
                696,
                958,
                800
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
